# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker does NOT read .gitignore. Without this file the whole backend/ tree is
# uploaded to the daemon on every build — 195 MB, including backend/.env with
# real secrets, dev-secrets.properties, 115 MB of target/ and 36 MB of uploaded
# documents (H-8).
#
# Strategy: deny everything, then re-admit only what the build needs. A new file
# dropped next to the Dockerfile is then excluded by default rather than shipped
# by default.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*

!pom.xml
!src/
!.mvn/

# ─── Re-denied inside the paths re-admitted above ────────────────────────────
# The JWT signing keypair is generated here for local development. "COPY src
# ./src" hands it to Maven, which copies src/main/resources/** into the jar, so
# every image shipped BOOT-INF/classes/keys/jwt-private.pem. Production supplies
# the keypair through APP_JWT_PRIVATE_KEY / APP_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY instead (C-1).
**/keys/
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/*.jks

# ─── Redundant after "*", stated so the intent is readable ───────────────────
.env
.env.*
dev-secrets.properties
target/
uploads/
exports/
logs/
